// Raw Linux system-call harness: `@FFI.Syscall` exercised against a real kernel.
//
// Linux-only and LLVM-only, both by construction rather than by choice. A
// `@FFI.Syscall` is refused at compile time on a target that cannot reach the
// Linux kernel, and the interpreter has no instruction stream of its own to put
// `svc`/`syscall` in — so this suite has one command:
//
//   kira test --backend llvm tests-kik/syscall-harness
//
// main is trivial; the driver synthesized in test mode is the real entry.

import Foundation

@Main
function main() {
    return
}
